From d6e8c63c471fcd05f171e955fba44f1f942458de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bernhard=20Rosenkr=C3=A4nzer?= <bero@lindev.ch>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:30:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iconvdata: IBM1390/IBM1399 encoders must not read past the
 input (bug 34914)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GLIBC-SA-2026-0031 / CVE-2026-124024.  No Fix-Commit is on master.
The posted patch kept the check as inptr + 8 <= inend; the review asked
for a length comparison so the test does not form a pointer past the
object.  This backport uses that guard.

U+00E6 is a combining base.  The encoder looks four bytes ahead for the
next UCS-4 unit, but inptr + 4 < inend is true when only one to three
bytes follow, and get32 then reads past the buffer.  Require eight
bytes before looking ahead.  The pre-existing limitation of not storing
a split combining character in the shift state is unchanged.

Reported-by: slaythemole
Signed-off-by: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
